  "preamble": "Proto-Indo-European voiced aspirated *bʰ lost its aspiration in Proto-Germanic and, between vowels and after most consonants, was realized as the voiced bilabial fricative [β]; word-initially and after nasals it was a stop [b]. The fricative is the reconstructed medial value of Proto-Germanic *b, which Old English and Old Norse continue as [v] and Old High German hardened to b.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Deaspiration, Spirantization, Grimm's Law",
